<title>GERMANY: Rexrodt - shares must be held longer to avoid tax.</title>
<headline>Rexrodt - shares must be held longer to avoid tax.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany Economics Minister Guenter Rexrodt said on Monday he thought that the period for which shares should be held to avail of tax relief on speculative gains should be modestly extended.</p>
<p>Speaking at the official 1997 opening of the German bourse, Rexrodt said: &quot;When it comes to shares, any attempt to introduce a full tax on capital gains would nullify all our attempts to boost the risk-based capital markets.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;This would noticeably weaken Germany as a financial centre,&quot;Rexrodt said.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
